%! Using a module twice.
%!
%! Any Nemo program can be used as a module. Its @input and @parameter
%! directives declare what the using program provides, and @output what
%! the module returns. Here, the module is the input file hops.rls (see
%! "Input files" next to the run button), which `@use hops` reads.
%!
%! The example shows:
%! - how to use a module with @use, binding its input and parameter,
%! - how one module is used twice, under two names,
%! - how to read the output of a module as name::predicate.

@use hops { edge = flight, $limit = 1 } as direct .
@use hops { edge = flight, $limit = 3 } as short .

flight(berlin, dresden) .
flight(dresden, prague) .
flight(prague, vienna) .
flight(vienna, budapest) .

nonstop(?x, ?y) :- direct::within(?x, ?y) .
trip(?x, ?y) :- short::within(?x, ?y) .

@output nonstop, trip .
